  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSurface high pressure will remain centered off to our southeast \nthrough Thursday. This will result in dry and mostly clear \nconditions. \n\nWith good radiational cooling, will likely see some river valley fog\ndevelopment again tonight. Will also nudge temperatures down a bit \nthe next couple of nights and decrease afternoon dewpoints the next \ncouple afternoons. \n\nAs the airmass slowly moderates, afternoon temperatures will slowly \ntrend warmer each day. By Friday afternoon highs will be in the mid \nto possibly upper 60s. \n\nThe next chance of rain looks to be early next week as a low \npressure system approaches from the west.",
